    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0586" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg372"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 159.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr.
                        Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 183.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 21, 1871</date>. (Received February
                    11.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I inclose to you to day the orignal of a
                    letter which I have received from Count Bismarck, replying to your note of
                    November 21 to Baron Gerolt, and also a translation of the same. I have this day
                    received from Mr. Washburne a letter dated January 16, and I am more and more
                    convinced that no obstacle is opposed by the German government to delay the
                    transmission of your correspondence with our minister at Paris. * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d177-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
